+By default, Doc Detective scans the current directory for valid tests, but you can specify one or more test files with the `--input` argument. Separate multiple paths with commas. `--input` always sets `config.input` to an array: each comma-separated path is trimmed, `http://` and `https://` URLs are passed through unchanged, and all other paths are resolved to absolute paths with `path.resolve`. For example, to run tests in a file named `doc-content-inline-tests.md`, run the following command:
 
 ```bash
 npx doc-detective --input doc-content-inline-tests.md
 ```
 
+To run tests in multiple files, pass a comma-separated list:
+
+```bash
+npx doc-detective --input doc-content-inline-tests.md,another-test.md
+```
+
